 able to  talk to my heart's content about lore  analysis and whatever else seems  important so do expect a lot of Dark  Souls 1 talk on my channel in the future  I'll try to keep things fresh and offer  new perspectives I know that you all  don't want to hear repeat of what  someone's already said and I really want  to make a lot of lore videos because the  stories nurdles 1 are some great ones  filled with mystery and emotion which  every Souls pain deserves to know now a  closing note before we get too hyped we  should be reminded that this reunited or  has not been affiliated with from  software at all they aren't doing the  room  there seems to be one team doing it for  the switch and another doing it for  everyone else this is a Bandai Namco  thing which was to be expected as  Miyazaki has said in the past that's  what would happen with any potential  remastered this means that if the  remaster teams get liberal with changes  and fixes especially concerning the  content of the game even if it has to do  with some of the not-so-good stuff parts  of the game's direction could be  compromised however from everything that  has come out so far which admittedly is  much it sounds like there will not be  any changes to the combat / enemy side  things this means that we should be  getting Dark Souls with all of its level  design and enemy successes but also its  flaws this is a remaster not a remake I  think that's a very fair trade-off I'll  take the bed of chaos and lost izalith  in return for keeping Dark Souls true to  what it was intended to be the remaster  will also come with the artorias of the  abyss dlc and owners of the prepare to  die edition on Steam we got the game at  half off price or that was originally  what was said Bandai Namco has now come  out and said that there won't be a  discount all games will be the same  price but they had an official image  saying the steam thing was half off so I  think the steam thing could still be  half off but maybe 